Subject: oci seccomp expose the syscall table and compile per-rule actions
Why: Hex's oci class compiles an OCI linux.seccomp profile to BPF with this crate and loads it in the container init. It needs the arch syscall-name tables without the json feature (it parses the OCI format itself). An OCI profile names an action per syscall group and can give one syscall argument rules of differing actions (the default profile refuses socket(AF_NETLINK, _, NETLINK_AUDIT) but allows every other socket) - which SeccompFilter::new's single filter-wide match action can't express; SyscallRules carries a per-rule on-match action and the syscall's own fallthrough, and with_syscall_rules installs it. Sizing each syscall's BPF block for the unconditional case allocates it once instead of growing it, on the container-start path. SeccompFilter::new keeps its signature and byte-for-byte BPF output (upstream tests pass).

